  "kind": "pptx",
  "title": "Binary Search Trees",
  "lang": "en",
  "pages": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Definition",
      "size": [
        13.333,
        7.5
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Definition",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            12.1,
            1.05
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "A BST is a binary tree where every node's left subtree holds smaller keys and its right subtree holds larger keys.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Duplicates are excluded, or handled by one documented rule.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "The ordering invariant holds recursively at every node.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        }
      ],
      "flags": {
        "text_layer": true
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Search",
      "size": [
        13.333,
        7.5
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Search",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            12.1,
            1.05
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Compare the target with the root: go left if smaller, right if larger.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "The cost is Θ(h), where h is the height of the tree.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "A balanced tree has h = Θ(log n); a degenerate chain has h = n.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        }
      ],
      "flags": {
        "text_layer": true
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Insertion",
      "size": [
        13.333,
        7.5
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Insertion",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            12.1,
            1.05
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Search for the key until a null child is reached, then attach a new leaf.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Insertion never restructures an existing node.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "The running time equals the search time, Θ(h).",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        }
      ],
      "flags": {
        "text_layer": true
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Deletion",
      "size": [
        13.333,
        7.5
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Deletion",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            12.1,
            1.05
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "A leaf is removed directly.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "A node with one child is replaced by that child.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "A node with two children is replaced by its in-order successor, then that node is deleted.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        }
      ],
      "flags": {
        "text_layer": true
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "title": "Traversals",
      "size": [
        13.333,
        7.5
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Traversals",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            12.1,
            1.05
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Pre-order visits node, left, right; in-order visits left, node, right; post-order visits left, right, node.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "In-order traversal of a BST yields keys in sorted order.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Each traversal costs Θ(n) time and Θ(h) stack space.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        }
      ],
      "flags": {
        "text_layer": true
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "title": "Balanced Variants",
      "size": [
        13.333,
        7.5
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Balanced Variants",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            12.1,
            1.05
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "AVL trees keep the height difference between siblings at most 1 using rotations.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Red-black trees relax that rule but guarantee h <= 2 log2(n + 1).",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "C++ std::map and Java TreeMap are red-black trees.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        }
      ],
      "flags": {
        "text_layer": true
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "title": "Building a Balanced Tree",
      "size": [
        13.333,
        7.5
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Building a Balanced Tree",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.6,
            0.45,
            12.1,
            1.05
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Sort the keys, then take the middle element as the root of each subtree.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "This builds a height-balanced BST in Θ(n log n), dominated by the sort.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet",
          "text": "Inserting pre-sorted keys into a plain BST produces a chain, so balance first.",
          "level": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.85,
            1.85,
            11.6,
            5.0
          ]
        }
      ],
      "flags": {
        "text_layer": true
      }
    },
    {
